# kbdlight.schema — which layer may decide each key of the `kbdlight` subsystem.
#
# Read by /usr/lib/w/w-conf-lib.sh (and its Python twin) during the load
# pass; a user-layer assignment to a `system` key is dropped with a warning, and
# `wconf_set` refuses to write it in the first place. See update-system.md
# (decision 3) and w-conf.md.
#
# Format: <KEY>\t<scope>       scope: system | user | both
#   system — root domain: the admin (or fleet policy) decides, per machine.
#   user   — the logged-in user may override it in ~/.config/w/kbdlight.conf.
#   both   — either layer may speak; the usual priority order applies.

# The boot level is baked into the initramfs — a machine-wide artifact one user
# must not be able to rewrite, and changing it needs root anyway (image rebuild).
BOOT_LEVEL	system

# Which physical LED is "the keyboard backlight" is a fact about the hardware,
# not a preference.
DEVICE	system

# How far one keypress moves the level is pure personal feel, and changing it
# has never needed root.
STEP	user
